{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>He shall not see me.</b> With a kamatz, like ואומר אין רואני (Isaiah 47:10), להוציאנו ממצרים (Exodus 14:11), אם שוב ישיבני ד׳ (II Samuel 15:5)." "<b>And the meaning of 'and live'.</b> Is like 'and he shall live,' for he would die immediately, for Manoah said, 'Because we shall see the angel, we shall die' — 'for Elohim have we seen' (Judges 13:22), and Jacob too said, 'for I have seen Elohim face to face and my soul was delivered' (Genesis 32:31), how much more so the honored HaShem. And others say: 'a man shall not see me' — rather, he shall live forever, and this is the opposite of the language. And others say that the word לא serves in place of אחר, and so it is: not 'a man shall see me' but 'the living,' and the meaning is: the angels."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:08.298701425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}